From 1c885498fbe899c5809b531c81a174e6f97cf9eb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 21:26:39 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] windowing/gbm: a move to another output keeps the output it
 leaves on for its sound

Two holes that the commit before this one left in a move of Kodi to another
output of its device (CWinSystemGbm::MoveOutputTo(), PlanOutputMove(),
TestOutputMove(), the commit of the move):

- The output that Kodi left went off always, also when its sound was in use
  (the TV whose audio output is the one in use, when Kodi moves its picture to a
  monitor) or when hades-keep-outputs named it. Now, where it is kept on for its
  sound, the move goes to a CRTC that is off and can show Kodi on the output it
  moves to (KEEP_OUTPUTS::FreeCrtcForMove(): never the one in use, never one
  that is on), so that the output left keeps its own; and the commit of the move
  leaves it there black, its planes detached, as the other outputs kept on are
  left, in the order of KEEP_OUTPUTS::KeepModes() asked of the driver first
  (TEST_ONLY). Only black: as it was, it would show the buffer that Kodi showed
  on it last, which Kodi goes on drawing its next frames into; where the driver
  does not take it black (amdgpu needs a plane on a CRTC that is on), it goes off
  as before, and the log says why (KEEP_OUTPUTS::LeftOutputStays()). Where no
  CRTC that is off fits, the move takes the CRTC it always took, and the output
  left goes off, said too. For that, the output that Kodi draws on is now kept in
  the set of outputs whose sound is in use as well (it is not said in the log, it
  is on anyway).
- A move before the outputs that Kodi does not use were first turned off (the
  first 10 s, or longer while the turning off waits for the audio engine) had
  only the file. It now decides with the outputs that carry the sound in use
  when the audio engine has said them (the other devices are asked what they
  drive and closed again: nothing of them was turned off yet), and keeps to the
  file while the turning off would still wait (DecideSoundBeforeMove()). After
  that first turning off, a move uses the decision as it is, made again first
  where the engine has said other outputs since.

kodi.log, at info level unless a warning is said:
  "PlanOutputMove: HDMI-A-1 is kept on for its sound (the sound in use): Kodi
   moves to DP-1 on CRTC <id>, another than its own, so that it can stay on"
  "LogKeptOutputs: HDMI-A-1 stay(s) on, black, for its sound (the sound in use)"
  warning "PlanOutputMove: HDMI-A-1 is kept on for its sound (...), but no CRTC
   that is off can show Kodi on DP-1: it goes off with the move"
  warning "LogKeptOutputs: HDMI-A-1, which Kodi leaves, goes off with the move
   although it is kept on for its sound (...): the driver needs a plane on a CRTC
   that is on, and as it was it would show the buffer that Kodi showed on it
   last, which Kodi goes on drawing into"
  "DecideSoundBeforeMove: the audio engine has not said yet which audio output
   it uses: in this move, only hades-keep-outputs keeps outputs on"

Tested on the host: the choice of the CRTC and when the output left stays on
(86 checks with those of the commit before; sixteen mutations of the header,
each caught); the tests of hades-keep-outputs still pass (50). The commits of a
move are read and syntax-checked against the build's own compile commands;
whether each driver takes the output left black on its CRTC, only hardware
shows.
